  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Deuteronomy",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 21,
    "summary": "How amends are made for murders by unknown persons—Equity is required in dealing with wives and children—Stubborn and rebellious sons will be put to death.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "If one be found slain in the land which the Lord thy God giveth thee to possess it, lying in the field, and it be not known who hath slain him:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 6
          },
          {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 107
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:1",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Then thy elders and thy judges shall come forth, and they shall measure unto the cities which are round about him that is slain:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "OR the distance to."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 97
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:2",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And it shall be, that the city which is next unto the slain man, even the elders of that city shall take an heifer, which hath not been wrought with, and which hath not drawn in the yoke;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 136,
            "end": 143,
            "text": "OR worked."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 21
          },
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 39
          },
          {
            "start": 150,
            "end": 153
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:3",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And the elders of that city shall bring down the heifer unto a rough valley, which is neither eared nor sown, and shall strike off the heifer’s neck there in the valley:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "HEB plowed, worked."
          },
          {
            "start": 120,
            "end": 126,
            "text": "OR break."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:4",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And the priests the sons of Levi shall come near; for them the Lord thy God hath chosen to minister unto him, and to bless in the name of the Lord; and by their word shall every controversy and every stroke be tried:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 200,
            "end": 206,
            "text": "OR case of assault."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 210,
            "end": 216
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:5",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And all the elders of that city, that are next unto the slain man, shall wash their hands over the heifer that is beheaded in the valley:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 122,
            "text": "OR whose neck is broken."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 41
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 66
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:6",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And they shall answer and say, Our hands have not shed this blood, neither have our eyes seen it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 97
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:7",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Be merciful, O Lord, unto thy people Israel, whom thou hast redeemed, and lay not innocent blood unto thy people of Israel’s charge. And the blood shall be forgiven them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "HEB Let atonement be made for."
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "Ps. 25:22; D&C 84:99 (99–100)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:8",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "So shalt thou put away the guilt of innocent blood from among you, when thou shalt do that which is right in the sight of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 35
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 99
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:9",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "When thou goest forth to war against thine enemies, and the Lord thy God hath delivered them into thine hands, and thou hast taken them captive,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:10",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And seest among the captives a beautiful woman, and hast a desire unto her, that thou wouldest have her to thy wife;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:11",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Then thou shalt bring her home to thine house; and she shall shave her head, and pare her nails;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:12",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And she shall put the raiment of her captivity from off her, and shall remain in thine house, and bewail her father and her mother a full month: and after that thou shalt go in unto her, and be her husband, and she shall be thy wife.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "OR captive garb."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:13",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And it shall be, if thou have no delight in her, then thou shalt let her go whither she will; but thou shalt not sell her at all for money, thou shalt not make merchandise of her, because thou hast humbled her.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "Deut. 24:7."
          },
          {
            "start": 155,
            "end": 178,
            "text": "HEB treat her harshly."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Deut. 24:7.",
            "prettyString": "Deuteronomy 24:7",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "deuteronomy",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 24,
                    "end": 24,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 7,
                        "end": 7
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:14",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "If a man have two wives, one beloved, and another hated, and they have born him children, both the beloved and the hated; and if the firstborn son be hers that was hated:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "OR despised, disliked (also vv. 16–17). Gen. 29:33."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 94
          },
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 128
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:15",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Then it shall be, when he maketh his sons to inherit that which he hath, that he may not make the son of the beloved firstborn before the son of the hated, which is indeed the firstborn:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "HEB prefer."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 57
          },
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 77
          },
          {
            "start": 156,
            "end": 171
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Deuteronomy 21:16",
        "book": "Deuteronomy",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "But he shall acknowledge the son of the hated for the firstborn, by giving him a double portion of all that he hath: for he is the beginning of his strength; the right of the firstborn is his.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 2:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 127,
            "end": 130,
            "text": "OR his first issue."
          },
          {
            "start": 131,
            "end": 140,
            "text": "Gen. 49:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 175,
            "end": 184,
            "text": "TG Firstborn."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 49
          },
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 126
          },
          {
            "start": 185,
